{{Quote|The blood of all Taris will not be on my hands. If it's war you want, you'll fight alone!|Tynnra Pamlo|<ref name="R1 novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref>}}
'''Taris''' was a polluted [[City|urban]] [[planet]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]. Although Taris was a heavily populated [[ecumenopolis]], much of the surface itself was polluted with wrecked [[starship]]s and dense, overgrown [[swamp]]s. Makeshift tenements made of shipping containers and crashed starships stacked on top of one another, while [[Color|yellow]] smog drifted in the [[atmosphere]]. The elite of the planet dwelled in nicer [[skyscraper]]s.

==Description==
[[File:Otor-Hub-CLNE.png|thumb|250px|left|Taris was located in the Outer Rim Territories]]
Taris was an polluted [[ecumenopolis]] [[planet]]<ref name="Empire's End" /> located in the [[Taris system]]<ref name="Squad Goals 1" /> of the [[Taris sector]], a [[Sector|subsector]] of the [[Ojoster sector]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].The planet was situated in grid square I-8 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Appendix" /> Taris was a very diverse [[city]] that was covered in both urban sprawl and wastelands. On the far side dwelled the wealthy and middle classes. Wealthy citizens lived in massive towers guarded by private security forces, which were surrounded by cities filled with middle class residents. On the opposite side, poorer inhabitants lived in squalor in wastelands such as the former [[Talinn district]]. The Talinn district was covered by decaying urban infrastructure, wrecked starships, and old shipping containers. Additionally, Talinn was overgrown with [[three-fingered vine]]s and [[slime-slick fungus]].<ref name="Empire's End" /> According to [[Runa Blask]] &mdash; a [[Togruta]] native of Taris<ref name="Runa Blask Databank">{{Databank|runa-blask|Runa Blask}}</ref> &mdash; the planet was home to criminal outfits that made the [[Slugrats]] of [[Courtsilius]] look like a "after-school programs from talented youths" in comparison.<ref name="Zero Company">''[[Star Wars Zero Company]]''</ref> Purple was considered a traditional color of administration on Taris.<ref name="TFA Visual Dictionary" />

==History==
===Early history and Clone Wars===
{{Quote|We have a sighting that places Enigma on a ''Providence''-class dreadnought. We're currently investigating rumors that this ship is about to attack Taris.|Wullf Yularen, to the Jedi High Council|<ref name="Dark Disciple">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref>}}
At some point in [[The galaxy|galactic]] [[Timeline of galactic history|history]], Taris suffered from a [[Devastation of Taris|devastation]], resulting in the surface being littered with [[Starship|ships]], many buildings being destroyed, and the [[atmosphere]] becoming largely polluted. Although the [[city]] ultimately maintained its status as a major urban [[Planet|world]], much of its population resorted to living in makeshift homes, many of which were old shipping containers.<ref name="Empire's End" />

During the [[Clone Wars]], Taris was represented in the [[Galactic Senate]] by [[Senator]] [[Kin Robb]].<ref name="Join the Battle" /> Near the end of the war, [[Admiral]] [[Wullf Yularen]] received rumors that [[Count]] [[Dooku]]'s new right-hand "Admiral Enigma" (the fallen [[Jedi Master]] [[Quinlan Vos]]) was planning to attack Taris with his [[Providence-class Dreadnought|''Providence''-class Dreadnought]]. As a result, the [[Jedi High Council]] authorized a [[Rescue of Quinlan Vos|mission]] to rescue Vos from [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] captivity.<ref name="Dark Disciple" />

===Ages of the Empire and New Republic===
In [[17 BBY]], anti-Imperial insurgent [[Saw Gerrera]] met up with [[Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa]] on Taris, where Gerrera reported to him the success of a Gerrera-led [[Mission to Gyndine|mission]] with six other [[Onderon]]ian [[Partisans]] to [[Gyndine]] two days earlier. The objective was to infiltrate the [[Central Medical Facility]] and install a [[transmitter]] inside the medical network to spy on Imperial intelligence. To gain access to the facility, Gerrera had his friends killed and drugged himself to appear dead temporarily, so they would be carried into the medcenter. Gerrera then impersonated an Imperial officer and shut down power to the hospital, to ensure the planted node would not be rejected by the system. On Taris, Organa admonished the Partisan for the deaths incurred in powering down the hospital, to which Gerrera replied that he also lost loved ones, but the mission made it worth it. Gerrera then left for [[Coruscant]] to help the [[Erso family]].<ref name="SawGerrera1">[[Rogue One – Saw Gerrera 1|''Rogue One – Saw Gerrera'' 1]]</ref> 

[[File:RO_trailer_Pamlo.png|thumb|right|200px|Senator Tynnra Pamlo represented Taris in the Imperial Senate.]]
Five [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|founding]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], a ship made a quick jump to Taris before quickly leaving the [[Star system|system]] for [[Thustra]]. The vessel then rendezvoused with a group of [[Berch Teller's rebel cell|rebels]], who had [[Mission to Murkhana|commandeered]] [[Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]]'s ship, the ''[[Carrion Spike]]''.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> Around the time of the [[Battle of Scarif]], Taris was represented in the [[Imperial Senate]] by Senator [[Tynnra Pamlo]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

In the [[Standard month|months]] following the [[Battle of Endor]], a cabal of [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] adherents known as the [[Acolytes of the Beyond]] bought the late [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader's]] supposed [[Darth Vader's lightsaber|lightsaber]], intending to destroy it to return it to its master in [[death]].<ref name="Aftermath" /> In [[5 ABY]], the [[New Republic]] operatives [[Norra Wexley]], [[Sinjir Rath Velus]], and [[Jas Emari]] lured the [[bounty hunter]] [[Mercurial Swift]] into a [[Capture of Mercurial Swift|trap]] on Taris' wasteland. They questioned him for information on [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]] before releasing him. In response, Swift sought to capture a [[bounty]] on Emari's head.<ref name="Empire's End" />

Thirty years after the Battle of [[Endor]], Taris was represented by [[Andrithal Robb-Voti]] in the [[New Republic Senate]] on [[Hosnian Prime]].<ref name="TFA Visual Dictionary" />

==Behind the scenes==
Taris was first [[canon]]ically mentioned in the [[2014]] novel [[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']] by [[James Luceno]],<ref name="Tarkin" /> and first appeared in the [[2015]] novel [[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']], written by [[Chuck Wendig]].<ref name="Aftermath" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, [[Taris/Legends|Taris]] was created for and first appeared in the [[2003]] [[Wikipedia:Role-playing game|role-playing game]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic]]''.<ref name="KOTOR">''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic]]''</ref>

A preview of [[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 1]] included in ''[[The High Republic Free Digital Sampler]]'' had Taris highlighted on an included [[The galaxy|galaxy]] map.<ref name="Sampler">''[[The High Republic Free Digital Sampler]]''</ref> In the final comic, other worlds were highlighted instead.<ref name="HRA 1">[[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 1]]</ref>

